("How can commercial banks accurately predict the daily cash demand of individual ATMs using historical) Tj
T* (withdrawal patterns, calendar attributes, and short-term rolling velocity, so as to minimize idle cash holding costs) Tj
T* (and completely prevent service outages?") Tj
T* (  ) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (  ) Tj
T* (    In specific operational terms, the challenges being solved in this project encompass:) Tj
T* (  ) Tj
T* (  ) Tj
T* (    ) Tj
T* (      Non-Stationary Demand Patterns: Cash withdrawal is inherently irregular. A kiosk situated near a commercial) Tj
T* (corporate park experiences high demand Monday through Friday and low demand on weekends. Conversely, a) Tj
T* (kiosk in a tourist area or shopping district spikes on Saturdays and Sundays.) Tj
T* (    ) Tj
T* (    ) Tj
T* (      Calendar and Holiday Volatility: National holidays, bank holidays, and festive seasons trigger sudden surges in) Tj
T* (cash withdrawals. Static weekly schedules cannot accommodate fluctuating calendar dates.) Tj
T* (    ) Tj
T* (    ) Tj
T* (      Information Lag in Kiosk Monitoring: While ATM telemetry reports current cassette balance, it lacks) Tj
T* (␀p␀r␀e␀d␀i␀c␀t␀i␀v␀e␀ ␀f␀o␀r␀e␀s␀i␀g␀h␀t␀ ␀r␀e␀g␀a␀r␀d␀i␀n␀g␀ ␀w␀h␀e␀t␀h␀e␀r␀ ␀t␀h␀e␀ ␀r␀e␀m␀a␀i␀n␀i␀n␀g␀  ¹␀2␀,␀0␀0␀,␀0␀0␀0␀ ␀w␀i␀l␀l␀ ␀l␀a␀s␀t␀ ␀4␀ ␀h␀o␀u␀r␀s␀ ␀o␀r␀ ␀3␀ ␀d␀a␀y␀s␀ ␀u␀n␀d␀e␀r␀ ␀p␀r␀e␀v␀a␀i␀l␀i␀n␀g␀ ␀l␀o␀c␀a␀l) Tj
T* (conditions.) Tj
T* (    ) Tj
T* (    ) Tj
T* (      High Variance in Surge Withdrawals: Extreme high-demand episodes \(e.g., Diwali, Eid, Christmas, or) Tj
T* (month-beginning pension/salary credit days\) deviate sharply from regular distributions, presenting significant) Tj
T* (forecasting challenges.) Tj
