(In time-series tabular regression, feature engineering is the most critical determinant of model predictive) Tj
T* (capability. Because the raw data only logged date, ATM identifier, and withdrawal amount, domain-specific) Tj
T* (features were engineered to provide temporal context and local demand momentum:) Tj
T* (  ) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (  15.1 Derivation of Key Predictive Features) Tj
T* (  ) Tj
T* (    ) Tj
T* (      1. Previous Day Demand \(Lag-1 Feature\)) Tj
T* (      ) Tj
T* (        Formulated as: df['prev_day_demand'] = df.groupby\('atm_id'\)['cash_demand'].shift\(1\). ) Tj
T* (        Provides the immediate baseline of current consumption velocity.) Tj
T* (      ) Tj
T* (    ) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (    ) Tj
T* (      2. Previous 7-Day Average Demand \(Rolling Mean\)) Tj
T* (      ) Tj
T* (        Formulated as: df['prev_7day_avg'] = df.groupby\('atm_id'\)['cash_demand'].shift\(1\).rolling\(window=7,) Tj
T* (min_periods=7\).mean\(\). ) Tj
T* (        Smooths high-frequency day-to-day fluctuations while capturing weekly localized spending trends.) Tj
T* (      ) Tj
T* (    ) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (    ) Tj
T* (      3. Calendar Temporal Decomposition) Tj
T* (      ) Tj
T* (        Extracted df['weekday'] = df['date'].dt.weekday \(0 to 6\) and df['month'] = df['date'].dt.month \(1 to 12\) to) Tj
T* (allow tree splits to segment weekend vs. weekday demand and month-end salary cycles.) Tj
T* (      ) Tj
T* (    ) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (    ) Tj
T* (      4. Working Day vs. Holiday Binary Classification) Tj
T* (      ) Tj
T* (        Integrated statutory banking holiday calendars mapped with weekends to create a clean binary flag: 1 for) Tj
T* (standard business operating days, 0 for bank holidays, festivals, or weekend shutdowns.) Tj
T* (      ) Tj
T* (    ) Tj
T* (  ) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (  ) Tj
T* (    Following the application of the 7-day rolling shift, the initial 7 burn-in records per ATM were trimmed,) Tj
T* (yielding the definitive, high-integrity dataset of 570,425 records.) Tj
