T* (      An R² score of 0.4703 denotes moderate predictive performance. In academic literature and commercial) Tj
T* (banking practice, ATM cash demand is widely recognized as a highly stochastic, non-stationary time series) Tj
T* (influenced by unobserved external variables—such as nearby competitor ATM outages, spontaneous local retail) Tj
T* (sales, unexpected bank branch closures, emergency medical expenses, and cash-in-circulation macroeconomic) Tj
T* (trends. Given that the system relies on only six fundamental tabular features without accessing private customer) Tj
T* (account balances or real-time footfall cameras, achieving an R² of ~0.47 across 114,085 testing instances is) Tj
T* (practical, robust, and completely devoid of artificial data leakage or overfitting.) Tj
